---
title: 20-Minute One-Pan Mince
servings: 2
course: dinner
time: 20m
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/BGG7UWZ1YTw/maxresdefault.jpg
tags: quick, one-pan, beef, rice
source: https://youtu.be/BGG7UWZ1YTw
---

Once your @oil{1%tbsp} is hot in a #pan{}, add @mince{500%g}. Season with @salt{} and don't touch it.

Dice @red onion{1} and @tomato{3%small}. Crush and finely dice @garlic{1%clove}.

Add the diced onion to the beef. Stir the beef up, breaking it up at the same time, until you get some good color on the bottom of the meat.

Add the tomatoes and the garlic to the pan.

Season with @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @ground coriander{1%tsp}, @garlic powder{1%tsp}, @cumin{1%tsp}, @garam masala{1%tsp}, and @chilli powder{1%tsp}. Give everything a good stir.

Cover with a #lid and simmer for ~{4-5%minutes}.

Add @frozen peas{1%cup} and stir them through.

Add @water{0.5%cup} and simmer for another ~{2%minutes}.

Serve over @cooked rice{} with some chopped @?coriander{}.
